## Why This Is Asked

Tests understanding of streaming architectures under load, including partitioning, backpressure, and correctness guarantees (exactly-once) in the presence of late data and failures.

## Key Concepts

- Backpressure and bounded queues
- Partitioning by key for ordering guarantees
- Watermarks and late-data handling
- Windowed aggregations and state management
- Exactly-once semantics via checkpointing and replay
- Test strategies for bursts, late data, and crash recovery

## Code Example

```javascript
// Pseudo-code: per-partition window with watermark and late path
class PartitionProcessor {
  constructor(sensorId, queueCapacity = 1000) {
    this.sensorId = sensorId;
    this.queue = new BoundedQueue(queueCapacity);
    this.window = new TumblingWindow(5000); // 5s window
    this.watermark = new MonotonicWatermark();
    this.lateBuffer = new LateDataBuffer();
  }

  process(event) {
    if (event.timestamp < this.watermark.get()) {
      this.lateBuffer.add(event);
      return;
    }

    if (this.queue.isFull()) {
      this.signalBackpressure();
      return false;
    }

    this.queue.add(event);
    this.watermark.update(event.timestamp);
    this.window.add(event);

    if (this.window.isReady()) {
      this.emitAggregates();
      this.window.reset();
    }
  }
}
```

